.TH CHRONICLED 8 "2026-07-24" "chronicle 1.0" "InterGenOS System Administration"
.SH NAME
chronicled \- Chronicle backup engine and sentinel
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B chronicled
[\fB\-\-config\fR \fIFILE\fR]
[\fB\-\-task\fR \fITASK\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B chronicled
is the privileged backup engine. In its default
.B serve
task it runs as a long-running system service: it owns all capture, retention,
restore, and verification, exposes the verb surface on the root-owned socket
.IR /run/chronicle/engine.sock ,
and runs a poll-based watcher that captures the config-state layer when
\fI/etc\fR changes on disk. It is started at boot by
.IR chronicled.service .
.PP
Non-default tasks are the entry points the timer and restore units invoke:
.TP
.B \-\-task capture-userdata
Hourly user-data capture (\fIchronicle-userdata.timer\fR). A quiet no-op when
the target is absent; a change larger than the off-peak threshold is enqueued.
.TP
.B \-\-task drain-queue
Drain the deferred-capture queue during the off-peak window
(\fIchronicle-offpeak.timer\fR); a fire inside working hours is a no-op.
.TP
.B \-\-task scrub
Weekly integrity scrub (\fIchronicle-scrub.timer\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-task restore \-\-request \fIFILE\fR
Apply a restore from a request file, run by the higher-capability
.I chronicle-restore@.service
leg. The request JSON carries the layer, version, paths, and mode; the result
is written to the sibling \fIFILE\fR with a \fI.result.json\fR suffix.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-config " \fIFILE\fR"
Path to
.BR chronicle.conf (5)
(default \fI/etc/chronicle/chronicle.conf\fR).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/chronicle/
Always-on local store and durable capture-intent queue.
.TP
.I /run/chronicle/engine.sock
Line-delimited-JSON IPC socket, owned
.BR root:chronicle ", mode " 0660 ,
in a directory of mode
.BR 0750 .
.TP
.I /usr/lib/sysusers.d/chronicle.conf
Declares the
.B chronicle
group.
.SH SECURITY
The always-on sentinel runs at a deliberately low capability set \(em
.B CAP_DAC_READ_SEARCH
only (read every user's home for capture, write nothing outside the store) with
.B ProtectHome=read-only
and a strict
.BR ProtectSystem .
Restore needs to recreate ownership and mode, so it runs in a separate,
higher-capability transient unit
.RB ( chronicle-restore@.service :
.BR CAP_CHOWN ", " CAP_FOWNER ", " CAP_DAC_OVERRIDE )
rather than granting those powers to the always-on daemon.
.PP
Access to the engine is gated twice, and the two gates answer different
questions.
.PP
First, the socket is
.BR root:chronicle ", mode " 0660 ,
so only root and the accounts in the
.B chronicle
group can open it at all. That decision is the kernel's and is made before a
byte is read \(em polkit cannot make it, because polkit is only consulted once a
caller has already connected. The engine applies the ownership and mode as the
socket is created, under a umask that denies every bit outside the owner, and
reads the result back off the inode before serving; a socket whose permissions
do not verify is narrowed to owner-only. If the
.B chronicle
group does not exist the socket stays owner-only and the engine says so in the
journal \(em it never falls back to a wider mode.
.PP
Second, every non-root peer is authorized per request against one of two polkit
actions, at the tier the requested verb needs:
.BR org.intergenos.Chronicle.read
for backup health and version metadata
.RB ( status ", " queue-status ", " list ", " target-scan ),
and
.B org.intergenos.Chronicle.manage
for everything else. The split is by disclosure, not by whether a verb writes:
.BR manifest ", " diff ", " verify " and " restore-plan
read only, but their answers carry file paths out of a store that holds every
user's home directory, so they stay administrative. Read-tier answers have their
one path-bearing field (a queued intent's
.BR scope )
stripped. A refused read is never escalated to the administrative action, so a
read can never raise a password dialog. Both tiers fail closed \(em an
unauthorized or unverifiable peer is refused. Root peers (the CLI under sudo,
the
.BR pkm (1)
pre-transaction handler) are already privileged and skip the check.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR chronicle (1),
.BR chronicle.conf (5),
.BR pkm (1)
